{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791104193200,"sessionID":"ses_ef9df0448ffeLrzFg2kCTVuW9n","part":{"partID":"prt_1062111380010Ch4VdemgFhoqC","sessionID":"ses_ef9df0448ffeLrzFg2kCTVuW9n","messageID":"msg_106210dda001MEoQyZPXNT3qHp","type":"tool","id":"call_01a10621110a71af95b9d95acb06c988","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/skill-up-2551750943/.opencode/skills/git-worktrees-prime-turbo-skill-upper/references/raw-git-commands.md"},"output":"Read file /tmp/skill-up-2551750943/.opencode/skills/git-worktrees-prime-turbo-skill-upper/references/raw-git-commands.md, lines 1-63\n1: # Raw Git commands\n2: \n3: Apply the main skill's ownership, preservation, and safety checks. Substitute all placeholders. Run only commands for the selected operation, including its prerequisite checks.\n4: \n5: ## Creation\n6: \n7: Inspect the source and selected base:\n8: \n9: ```sh\n10: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree list --porcelain -z\n11: # Only when <repo> is a checkout, not a bare repository.\n12: git -C \"<repo>\" status --short --branch\n13: git -C \"<repo>\" rev-parse --verify \"<base-ref>^{commit}\"\n14: \n15: # Only for a destination inside another checkout; require exit 0 before creation.\n16: git -C \"<enclosing-checkout>\" check-ignore -q -- \"<selected-relative-path>/\"\n17: ```\n18: \n19: Choose one creation alternative:\n20: \n21: ```sh\n22: # New branch, explicitly based on the selected commit/ref.\n23: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add -b \"<task-branch>\" \"<worktree>\" \"<base-ref>\"\n24: \n25: # Alternative: continue an existing branch that is not checked out elsewhere.\n26: # Require exit 0; do not let a missing local branch resolve to a remote branch.\n27: git -C \"<repo>\" show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/heads/<task-branch>\"\n28: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add \"<worktree>\" \"<task-branch>\"\n29: \n30: # Alternative: disposable inspection of a specific commit.\n31: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add --detach \"<worktree>\" \"<commit>\"\n32: ```\n33: \n34: Verify the resulting checkout and repeat any required ignore check:\n35: \n36: ```sh\n37: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse --show-toplevel\n38: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --branch\n39: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse HEAD\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ## Cleanup\n43: \n44: ```sh\n45: # Clean status does not establish preservation of ignored files or detached commits.\n46: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --branch --untracked-files=all\n47: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --ignored\n48: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse HEAD\n49: \n50: # Exit 0 proves this tip is an ancestor of this target. Other outcomes need review.\n51: git -C \"<repo>\" merge-base --is-ancestor \"<task-tip>\" \"<integration-ref>\"\n52: \n53: # Run from a surviving checkout or bare repository after the checks above.\n54: # Remove only if the cleanup decision tree permits checkout removal.\n55: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree remove \"<worktree>\"\n56: # Separately, delete the branch only if the branch-deletion conditions are met.\n57: git -C \"<repo>\" branch -d \"<task-branch>\"\n58: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree list --porcelain -z\n59: \n60: # Only for intentionally removed worktrees; review every dry-run entry before pruning.\n61: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree prune --dry-run --verbose\n62: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree prune --verbose\n63: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/skill-up-2551750943/.opencode/skills/git-worktrees-prime-turbo-skill-upper/references/raw-git-commands.md, lines 1-63\n1: # Raw Git commands\n2: \n3: Apply the main skill's ownership, preservation, and safety checks. Substitute all placeholders. Run only commands for the selected operation, including its prerequisite checks.\n4: \n5: ## Creation\n6: \n7: Inspect the source and selected base:\n8: \n9: ```sh\n10: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree list --porcelain -z\n11: # Only when <repo> is a checkout, not a bare repository.\n12: git -C \"<repo>\" status --short --branch\n13: git -C \"<repo>\" rev-parse --verify \"<base-ref>^{commit}\"\n14: \n15: # Only for a destination inside another checkout; require exit 0 before creation.\n16: git -C \"<enclosing-checkout>\" check-ignore -q -- \"<selected-relative-path>/\"\n17: ```\n18: \n19: Choose one creation alternative:\n20: \n21: ```sh\n22: # New branch, explicitly based on the selected commit/ref.\n23: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add -b \"<task-branch>\" \"<worktree>\" \"<base-ref>\"\n24: \n25: # Alternative: continue an existing branch that is not checked out elsewhere.\n26: # Require exit 0; do not let a missing local branch resolve to a remote branch.\n27: git -C \"<repo>\" show-ref --verify --quiet \"refs/heads/<task-branch>\"\n28: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add \"<worktree>\" \"<task-branch>\"\n29: \n30: # Alternative: disposable inspection of a specific commit.\n31: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree add --detach \"<worktree>\" \"<commit>\"\n32: ```\n33: \n34: Verify the resulting checkout and repeat any required ignore check:\n35: \n36: ```sh\n37: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse --show-toplevel\n38: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --branch\n39: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse HEAD\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ## Cleanup\n43: \n44: ```sh\n45: # Clean status does not establish preservation of ignored files or detached commits.\n46: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --branch --untracked-files=all\n47: git -C \"<worktree>\" status --short --ignored\n48: git -C \"<worktree>\" rev-parse HEAD\n49: \n50: # Exit 0 proves this tip is an ancestor of this target. Other outcomes need review.\n51: git -C \"<repo>\" merge-base --is-ancestor \"<task-tip>\" \"<integration-ref>\"\n52: \n53: # Run from a surviving checkout or bare repository after the checks above.\n54: # Remove only if the cleanup decision tree permits checkout removal.\n55: git -C \"<repo>\" worktree remove \"<worktree>\"\n56: # Separately, delete the branch only if the branch-deletion conditions are met.\n57: git -C \"<r